{
    "background_story": "Harlee was a brilliant sociologist who spent her career studying the works of \u00c9mile Durkheim. She became particularly fascinated with his concept of 'collective consciousness' and its impact on modern society. Harlee's research took her to various parts of the world, where she observed and documented the ways in which social norms and values shape individual behavior. Her book, 'The Durkheim Paradox,' explored the tension between individual freedom and social solidarity, sparking a new wave of interest in Durkheim's theories. As a professor, Harlee inspired a new generation of sociologists to think critically about the role of social structures in shaping human behavior. Her work was a testament to the enduring relevance of Durkheim's ideas, and she became known as one of the leading Durkheim scholars of her time.",
